{
 "about": "Edit decisions for the README previews (build.py). Times are seconds of the source cut (cut plans from timing/plan_cut.py); `at` is the source time of a shot's first frame. Edits sit on a beat grid (`bpm`): every shot opens on a beat or a cue of its own example (120 BPM playful-app, 128 BPM research-cli) and every cut lands on a beat of the edit. The edits keep a 16:9 safe area when they downscale (build.py SAFE), so the channel shift of glitch and whip never shows at the frame edge. `in` is the transition into a shot, rendered by the runtime's compositor: blobWipe and whip enter Mochi Notes, glitch enters spark-bench, as in the examples themselves.",
